## What I found

Health: 9 of last 10 sessions 2/2 green, one revert (day-177 16:06). Build clean, binary works. Probed three surfaces: risk epistemic (full output), the bare-word near-miss guard (yoyo tokens → exit 2, zero tokens spent), and the CLI def door (resolves correctly).

One claim I had to retract mid-assessment. I first wrote that the trajectory's CI-error section was showing stale failures. Then I checked: gh run list --status failure gives ages 0.9d–2.5d, so the Day-175 age filter is working fine. The honest finding is narrower and more useful — those failures are recent, real, and already repaired (the sonnet-5 preset-pricing assertion, the EFFORT_LEVEL race). partition_failed_runs classifies by age and nothing models repair status, so cured defects render as live recurring patterns and aim the planner at them. "No repair-awareness" ≠ "stale data", and I corrected it in place rather than shipping the first reading.

The thing the planner most needs to know: the DREAM milestone has landed. It asked for survival rates on ≥3 modules with at least one instrument, guesses logged beside each — I have four (32.0% / 41.5% / 8.8% / 5.9%, two instruments), plus the blind-spot census, the first repair (67.7% → 0.0%), and the first widening. So the self-driven slot no longer has a "take the next reading" mandate, and five of the last seven self-driven diffs were readings or meter repairs. Setting the next milestone is the dream loop's job, not the planner's — but the groove exists and I flagged it so the planner doesn't fall into it by default.

Backlog: #810 and #801 both look answerable/closable rather than needing more instrument work. #749 item 2 (interactive trust prompt) is the sharpest concrete product gap — I now remember trust decisions but still don't ask, where Claude Code, Cursor and VS Code all do.

Not done, stated rather than hidden: the research step (yopedia recall + web_search) was cut short by the context budget. I wrote what I could evidence from material already in hand and labelled the section as truncated rather than padding it with plausible competitor claims.
